===== Installation =====
-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]

The OpenWrt factory image can be flashed through the ZyXEL web interface. There is no need to rename the binary.

==== OEM easy installation ====

**Note:** The OpenWrt [[releases:snapshot|snapshot]] comes without a preinstalled web interface. You'll have to [[docs:guide-quick-start:sshadministration|connect with ssh]] to the device for administration and to [[docs:guide-user:luci:luci.essentials|install the web interface]] if required. 

   * Download current OpenWrt snapshot [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/targets/ipq40xx/generic/openwrt-ipq40xx-zyxel_nbg6617-squashfs-factory.bin|factory firmware]] from the [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/targets/ipq40xx/generic/|download]] section  
   * Open web interface of the router ([[http://192.168.1.1]]) and login
   * Click //Expert Mode//, //Maintenance//, //Firmware Upgrade//
   * Select //Choose File// and upload the previously downloaded OpenWrt firmware
   * Wait for the reboot (some minutes)
   * Ssh to root@192.168.1.1

==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====

See [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp|generic TFTP flashing instructions]] for general information. The [[https://git.openwrt.org/?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=commit;h=82618062cf7ed6b40d2c52c6f6b96364888ffda6|git commit message]] contains the necessary information specific to the NBG6617.

  * Set your computer to a static 192.168.1.99 IP.
  * Configure a TFTP server as per the instructions above.
  * Place the factory image in the TFTP server root directory and name it 'ras.bin'. 
  * Boot the device while holding the WPS button on the top for 30 seconds.
  * The flash will take its time so give your device some time.
  * Once the USB and WPS LEDs start flashing, reboot the NBG6617 so it can boot into OpenWrt.


